    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n64049" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Λῡδίζω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>speak Lydian</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hippon.
			</span></i> in <i><span class="en">
				<u>PSI</u>
				9.1089.1
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>play the Lydian</i>, of Magnes, in reference to his play called
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Λυδοί</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Eq.</u>
				523
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Λυδίζειν τὴν στολήν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Philostr.
					<u>VA</u>
					5.32
				</span></i>
			:—in <i><span class="en">
				Phot.
			</span></i> and <i><span class="en">
				Suid.
			</span></i> also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Λυδιάζω</span></b> .</div>
